cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its outputs, please cite it as below."
title: >-
  A Two-Stage Spatiotemporal Flood-Risk Framework with Flood-Aware Emergency
  Routing and Hybrid Quantum Dispatch for a Single-Orbit Coastal District
abstract: >-
  Reproducible research pipeline for flood-risk assessment and emergency response
  planning over Dakshina Kannada, Karnataka, India. Builds a multi-temporal
  Sentinel-1 SAR flood-frequency inventory under a single-orbit revisit
  constraint, trains a calibrated and SHAP-explainable static susceptibility
  model, modulates it with a rainfall-driven temporal trigger, routes emergency
  vehicles over a flood-aware OpenStreetMap graph with search-transparent
  Dijkstra and A*, and solves ambulance-to-incident dispatch as a QUBO with QAOA
  verified against the Hungarian optimum. Every reported figure and table is
  regenerated from source data by the included build system.
type: software
license: MIT
version: 1.0.0
